{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"7fcd628f","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# BGM rebuttal experiments: exact 3D Gaussian--OT gap + optional GPU proxy controls\n\nThis notebook is designed for the rebuttal concerns:\n\n1. **Broader bridge/coupling validation.** We vary coupling (Monge OT, noisy OT, independent) and bridge law (straight, Brownian) in a controlled 3D Euclidean Gaussian setting.\n2. **Proxy nature.** The 3D experiment computes the Markovization gap exactly from Gaussian conditional covariances, not from a kNN/PCA proxy.\n3. **Not just transport cost.** We include endpoint cost, velocity variance, normalized unexplained variance, and sampler-visible-state ablations.\n4. **Velocity / visible state precision.** The experiment uses the revised object\n   \\[\n   \\mathfrak G(\\mathscr Q,U,\\mathcal O)\n   =\n   \\int \\mathbb E \\operatorname{Tr}\\operatorname{Var}(U_t\\mid S_t)\\,dt,\n   \\qquad S_t=\\mathcal O_t(X_t).\n   \\]\n5. **GPU-capable optional image proxy.** The exact Gaussian experiment is CPU-only because it is small matrix algebra. The optional CIFAR/Fashion-MNIST proxy estimator uses PyTorch and will use CUDA if available.","metadata":{}},{"id":"65b9da8e","cell_type":"code","source":"# Imports and global settings\n\nimport os, math, json, time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = Path(\"/kaggle/working/bgm_rebuttal_outputs\") if Path(\"/kaggle\").exists() else Path(\"outputs_rebuttal\")\nOUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n# Integration window used in the reported exact values.\n# Keep this consistent with the paper/rebuttal tables.\nT_MIN = 0.05\nT_MAX = 0.95\nNUM_TIME = 2001\n\n# Brownian bridge variance parameter used in exact ablation.\nBROWNIAN_EPS = 0.5\n\nprint(\"Output directory:\", OUTPUT_DIR.resolve())","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.020186Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.020905Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.29623Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.020874Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.295385Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Output directory: /kaggle/working/bgm_rebuttal_outputs\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"id":"5cdc8bb0","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Exact Gaussian conditional-covariance computation\n\nFor a linear Gaussian bridge, stack all Gaussian variables into \\(Y\\). If\n\\[\nU_t=A_tY,\\qquad S_t=B_tY,\n\\]\nthen\n\\[\ng(t)\n=\n\\operatorname{Tr}\\left[\n\\Sigma_{UU}\n-\n\\Sigma_{US}\\Sigma_{SS}^{\\dagger}\\Sigma_{SU}\n\\right],\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\n\\Sigma_{UU}=A_t\\Sigma_YA_t^\\top,\\quad\n\\Sigma_{SS}=B_t\\Sigma_YB_t^\\top,\\quad\n\\Sigma_{US}=A_t\\Sigma_YB_t^\\top .\n\\]\nThe integrated gap over the same finite time window used by the image proxy is\n\\[\n\\int_{0.05}^{0.95} g(t)\\,dt .\n\\]\nThis is exact up to numerical quadrature.","metadata":{}},{"id":"c17c250d","cell_type":"code","source":"# Linear algebra utilities\n\ndef sqrtm_sym(M, eps=1e-12):\n    vals, vecs = np.linalg.eigh(M)\n    if np.min(vals) < -1e-9:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Matrix has negative eigenvalue {np.min(vals)}\")\n    vals = np.clip(vals, 0.0, None)\n    return vecs @ np.diag(np.sqrt(vals)) @ vecs.T\n\ndef random_orthogonal(seed=9, d=3):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    Q, _ = np.linalg.qr(rng.normal(size=(d, d)))\n    if np.linalg.det(Q) < 0:\n        Q[:, 0] *= -1\n    return Q\n\ndef trapz(y, x):\n    return np.trapezoid(y, x)\n\n# Rotated anisotropic target covariance.\n# Rotation makes projected-state ablations nontrivial while preserving eigenvalues.\nd = 3\nI = np.eye(d)\nR = random_orthogonal(seed=9, d=d)\neigvals = np.array([4.0, 2.0, 1.5])\nSigma = R @ np.diag(eigvals) @ R.T\n\nprint(\"Target covariance eigenvalues:\", np.linalg.eigvalsh(Sigma))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.297763Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.298185Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.321678Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.298161Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.320856Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Target covariance eigenvalues: [1.5 2.  4. ]\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"id":"8ff509ef","cell_type":"code","source":"# Coupling definitions with identical marginals:\n# Z ~ N(0,I), X ~ N(0,Sigma)\n# Coupling is determined by C = Cov(Z, X).\n\ndef coupling_covariance(kind, sigma=0.0):\n    if kind == \"monge\":\n        A = sqrtm_sym(Sigma)                 # X = A Z\n        C = A.T\n    elif kind == \"noisy\":\n        A = sqrtm_sym(Sigma - sigma**2 * I)  # X = A Z + sigma xi\n        C = A.T\n    elif kind == \"independent\":\n        C = np.zeros((d, d))\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(kind)\n    CovZX = np.block([[I, C], [C.T, Sigma]])\n    return CovZX\n\ndef endpoint_cost(CovZX):\n    # E ||X-Z||^2\n    A = np.concatenate([-I, I], axis=1)\n    return float(np.trace(A @ CovZX @ A.T))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.322707Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.323032Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.335Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.322985Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.334358Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":4},{"id":"bfa4bda1","cell_type":"code","source":"# Build linear maps U_t=A_U Y and S_t=B_S Y.\n\ndef maps_straight(t, P=None):\n    if P is None:\n        P = I\n    # Y = [Z, X]\n    A_U = np.concatenate([-I, I], axis=1)  # U = X-Z\n    A_Xt = np.concatenate([(1-t)*I, t*I], axis=1)\n    B_S = P @ A_Xt\n    return A_U, B_S\n\ndef maps_brownian(t, eps=BROWNIAN_EPS, P=None):\n    if P is None:\n        P = I\n    # Y = [Z, X, eta], eta ~ N(0,I)\n    # X_t=(1-t)Z+tX+sqrt(eps*t*(1-t)) eta\n    # U_t=(X-X_t)/(1-t)=X-Z-sqrt(eps*t/(1-t)) eta\n    s = math.sqrt(eps * t * (1-t))\n    q = math.sqrt(eps * t / (1-t))\n    A_U = np.concatenate([-I, I, -q*I], axis=1)\n    A_Xt = np.concatenate([(1-t)*I, t*I, s*I], axis=1)\n    B_S = P @ A_Xt\n    return A_U, B_S\n\ndef block_cov_for_bridge(CovZX, bridge):\n    if bridge == \"straight\":\n        return CovZX\n    elif bridge == \"brownian\":\n        return np.block([\n            [CovZX, np.zeros((2*d, d))],\n            [np.zeros((d, 2*d)), I]\n        ])\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(bridge)\n\ndef instantaneous_gap(CovY, A_U, B_S):\n    S_UU = A_U @ CovY @ A_U.T\n    S_SS = B_S @ CovY @ B_S.T\n    S_US = A_U @ CovY @ B_S.T\n    cond = S_UU - S_US @ np.linalg.pinv(S_SS) @ S_US.T\n    # symmetrize against numerical roundoff\n    cond = 0.5 * (cond + cond.T)\n    return float(np.trace(cond)), float(np.trace(S_UU))\n\ndef exact_gap(CovZX, bridge=\"straight\", P=None, t_min=T_MIN, t_max=T_MAX, num_time=NUM_TIME, eps=BROWNIAN_EPS):\n    t_grid = np.linspace(t_min, t_max, num_time)\n    CovY = block_cov_for_bridge(CovZX, bridge)\n    gaps, totals = [], []\n    for t in t_grid:\n        if bridge == \"straight\":\n            A_U, B_S = maps_straight(t, P=P)\n        elif bridge == \"brownian\":\n            A_U, B_S = maps_brownian(t, eps=eps, P=P)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(bridge)\n        g, total = instantaneous_gap(CovY, A_U, B_S)\n        gaps.append(g)\n        totals.append(total)\n    gap_auc = trapz(np.asarray(gaps), t_grid)\n    total_auc = trapz(np.asarray(totals), t_grid)\n    eta = gap_auc / total_auc if total_auc > 0 else np.nan\n    return {\n        \"gap\": float(gap_auc),\n        \"velocity_variance\": float(total_auc),\n        \"eta\": float(eta),\n        \"endpoint_cost\": endpoint_cost(CovZX),\n    }","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.336154Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.336422Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.353237Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.3364Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.352323Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":5},{"id":"ef6d3856","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Exact 3D Gaussian--OT table\n\nThis table addresses the proxy concern directly. It uses exact Gaussian conditional covariances instead of kNN/PCA. It also varies both endpoint coupling and bridge law.","metadata":{}},{"id":"ac2a2629","cell_type":"code","source":"coupling_specs = [\n    (\"Monge OT\", \"monge\", 0.0),\n    (\"noisy OT, sigma=0.3\", \"noisy\", 0.3),\n    (\"noisy OT, sigma=0.6\", \"noisy\", 0.6),\n    (\"noisy OT, sigma=1.0\", \"noisy\", 1.0),\n    (\"independent\", \"independent\", 0.0),\n]\n\nrows = []\nfor bridge in [\"straight\", \"brownian\"]:\n    for label, kind, sigma in coupling_specs:\n        CovZX = coupling_covariance(kind, sigma=sigma)\n        res = exact_gap(CovZX, bridge=bridge, P=I)\n        rows.append({\n            \"Bridge\": bridge,\n            \"Coupling\": label,\n            \"Endpoint cost\": res[\"endpoint_cost\"],\n            \"Velocity variance\": res[\"velocity_variance\"],\n            \"Exact gap\": max(res[\"gap\"], 0.0),\n            \"Normalized eta\": max(res[\"eta\"], 0.0),\n        })\n\ndf_exact = pd.DataFrame(rows)\ndisplay(df_exact)\n\ndf_exact.to_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"exact_3d_gaussian_ot_gap.csv\", index=False)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.355479Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.35632Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-24T17:06:30.0488Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-24T17:06:28.356287Z","shell.execute_reply":"202